@namespace PgmStudio.Client.Components

@* What the canvas shows, top-right and floating: the layer chips, then the view controls that end the row
   (fit / rotate), then the 2-D/3-D toggle in the very corner. Order is the row's meaning — a toggle that
   changes which layers exist at all sits outermost, past the layers it governs.

   It wraps rather than scrolls, so a narrow viewport stacks the chips upward instead of hiding the corner
   toggle behind an overflow. *@

<div class="canvas-layer-bar">@ChildContent</div>

@code {
    [Parameter] public RenderFragment? ChildContent { get; set; }
}
